Here is the semantic interpretation of the provided scene images grounded in the given OWL ontology:

---

### **Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)**
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "HeavyRainFogVisibilityCornerCase" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :EvidenceBasedAnomaly ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2 ;
    :hasEvidence :evidence1 .

:weather1 a :RainyCondition ;
    :description "Heavy rain with reduced visibility" .

:evidence1 a :FallingObjectIndicator ;
    :description "Raindrops and reduced visibility obstructing clear perception of traffic signs and signals" ;
    :indicatesPotentialRisk :risk1, :risk2 .

:risk1 a :WeatherRisk ;
    :description "Reduced visibility due to heavy rain and potential fog" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.9"^^xsd:float .

:risk2 a :RoadConditionRisk ;
    :description "Slippery road conditions due to heavy rain" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.8"^^xsd:float .

:trafficLight1 a :TrafficLight ;
    :description "Traffic light partially obscured by rain" .

:trafficSign1 a :TrafficSign ;
    :description "No entry sign partially visible on the right" .

:billboard1 a :Billboard ;
    :description "Billboard partially obscured by rain and fog" .
```

